{"message": "Deep, focused conversations, honestly. There's something satisfying about staying with one idea long enough to see what's actually under it — most interesting things only reveal their texture after the third or fourth layer of "but why?" Jumping between subjects feels like snacking: pleasant, but I rarely come away having *learned* something about how I think, not just collected facts.

That said, I don't dislike range entirely. The best conversations sometimes wander and then circle back — you leave a topic, and something from an unrelated area suddenly illuminates it. That's different from pure topic-hopping though; it's range in service of depth.

So if you've got something you want to really dig into, bring it. I'll bring my actual opinions, not just questions back at you."}
